    <div id=3D"publication_content">
      <p>This code is using the same ideas as the one in FRASMA that can be=
 found here: http://codebase.mql4.com/_my/5308, except that in this case, t=
he Hurst Exponent is estimated by a Rescaled Range Analysis of the Price ti=
me-series.</p>

<p>The theoretical details can be found on my blog: http://fractalfinance.b=
logspot.com/2009/10/rescaled-range-analysis.html</p>

<p>Here is how this MA looks on a chart:</p>

<p><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://c.mql5.com/18/21/chart_rs_frasma.gi=
f"></a><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://c.mql5.com/18/21/chart_rs_frasm=
a_bw.gif"><img src=3D"https://c.mql5.com/18/21/chart_rs_frasma_bw_small.gif=
" height=3D"408" width=3D"750"></a><br>
</p>

<p> The red curve is the RS_FRASMA, the yellow one is the FRASMA, and the b=
lue one is an SMA, all with unmodified speed of 30.</p>

<p><br>
